CI guard: [`catalog-completeness.test.ts`](../../src/lib/brand/catalog-completeness.test.ts) — every solidarity union and OPSEU sector must ship named collections, unique codes, a real `referenceUrl`, and **Other** (no “Additional unit” stubs).

CAAT Support FT/PT are distinct CAs (statutory split) but sit in the **same locals**, so Brand Kit ships one **College Support** identity. Hub seed still has two bargaining units for grievance/CA copy. [OPSEU PT certification (2016)](https://opseu.org/news/opseu-applies-to-represent-part-time-college-support-staff/14462/). CEC bargaining — [FT Support](https://www.collegeemployercouncil.ca/bargaining/full-time_support_staff_2025), [PT Support](https://www.collegeemployercouncil.ca/bargaining/part-time-support-staff-bargaining).

### CUPE

Starter reflects common **FT / PT / all-employee** patterns — employer-specific (OLRB may order either split).

- Coordinated multi-unit locals — [cupe.ca](https://cupe.ca/counterpoint/three-locals-one-goal-how-coordination-transformed-their-bargaining-strategy)
- PSE ~230 units — [Sector profile: Post-Secondary](https://cupe.ca/sector-profile-post-secondary)
- OLRB FT+PT vs all-employee — [Loyalist 1998](https://www.minicounsel.ca/olrb/1998/18288), [Kawartha Pine Ridge 1998](https://www.minicounsel.ca/olrb/1998/m125)

### Unifor

Single-unit **or** amalgamated (2+ bargaining units). ~40% amalgamated locals / ~80% of members.

- [Amalgamated locals guide (PDF)](https://www.unifor.org/sites/default/files/legacy/documents/document/unifor-amalgamatedlocals-en.pdf)
- [Servicing bargaining units (PDF)](https://www.unifor.org/sites/default/files/legacy/documents/document/unifor-servicingbargainingunits-en-print.pdf)

### USW

Amalgamated locals + **units** (unit chair).

- [Resolution 17: Amalgamation](https://usw.org/usw-convention/resolution-no-17-amalgamation/)
- [USW Local 1998 — multiple units](https://www.usw1998.ca/union-101/)

### ONA

Local = 1+ **employer bargaining units** (central + local CA).

- [Regions, Locals & Bargaining Units](https://ona.org/regions-locals-bargaining-units/)
- [How bargaining works](https://ona.org/how-bargaining-works/)

### PSAC

Treasury Board **classification groups** PA / TC / EB / SV are the familiar starter split; other employers use workplace names.

- [Our structure](https://psacunion.ca/our-structure-1)
- [Which bargaining unit am I in?](https://psacunion.ca/which-bargaining-unit-am-i-in)

## Do not

- Store catalog `referenceUrl` in Brand Kit JSON or membership URLs
- Treat Collection profiles as Hub `bargainingUnitId` tenancy
- Reintroduce CAAT FT/PT as `DEFAULT_BRAND_KIT` for every first visit
- Bundle another union’s official marks because OPSEU has a reference pack — see [`session-knowledge-2026-07-30-multi-union-sources.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-07-30-multi-union-sources.md)
